WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Praise the Lord! In more than forty years of marriage, we have experienced many testimonies of God.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Each experience has shown us that God is trustworthy.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
That is why we trust Him more and more.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Near the end of his life, Paul said, “I know whom I have believed.”

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:29.000
We also need to go through this process.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:38.000
We live in a microwave age, but not everything can be done in thirty seconds.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Growth in life takes time.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.000
We experience the Lord each day in our ordinary life.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Exodus records the tenth plague: darkness fell over Egypt.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:04.000
It was not an ordinary blackout, but darkness so deep one could not see.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Pharaoh summoned Moses.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Moses still would not agree to Pharaoh’s demand.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Pharaoh said, “Get away from me! The day you see my face again, you will die.”

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:37.000
If it had been his first time before Pharaoh, Moses might have been frightened.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:43.000
But by then, he had experienced God many times.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Moses knew that God was far greater than Pharaoh.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:57.000
At first Moses asked, “Who am I?” God said, “I will be with you.”

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Who I am is not what matters; God’s presence is what matters most.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Pharaoh again said that Moses would die if he saw him.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:18.000
Moses replied, “You will not see me, and I will not see you.”

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:25.000
Brothers and sisters, do not fear difficult circumstances.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Difficult circumstances can help us know God more.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Paul says in 2 Timothy, “I know whom I have believed.”

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:53.000
Pharaoh once said, “Who is Jehovah? I do not know Him.”

00:02:53.000 --> 00:03:00.000
But Moses came to know Jehovah and was convinced He could guard what had been entrusted to Him.
